{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/lem-genus-ideal-characterisation","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Lemma","doco:Section"],"label":"lem:genus-ideal-characterisation","kind":"lemma","title":"Genus-filtration ideal in Hecke coordinates","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/lem-genus-from-hecke-completeness","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/lem-chebyshev-degree-genus"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-genus-ideal-characterisation"],"tags":["seifert-surface","ideal","hecke-coordinates","truncation"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Archimedean.genus_ideal_characterisation","text":"genus-ideal-characterisation.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"lem:genus-ideal-characterisation\"></a><p>At genus <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">g = 4</code>, define the genus-filtration ideal <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{I}_4 := (u^5) \\subset \\mathbb{Z}[u]</code>. Then <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{I}_4</code> is the kernel of the truncation <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\pi_4 \\colon \\mathbb{Z}[u] \\to \\mathbb{Z}[u]/(u^5)</code>.</p>\n<p>This is the general fact that an ideal is the kernel of its quotient map. The reading of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{I}_4</code> as the terms in the Chebyshev expansion of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">a_p</code> whose Seifert cycles have no target in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H_1(\\Sigma_4)</code> is not part of this statement.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/genus-ideal-characterisation.md","heading":"Lemma","number":"8.12.1","page":"b/lem-genus-ideal-characterisation","qa":{"counts":{"pass":91,"fail":0,"warn":1,"na":12,"unknown":0,"stale":78},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.MassTheory.genus_ideal_characterisation","via":"ref","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/genus_ideal_characterisation.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
